From: CoreELEC Xiaomi SMB3 Multichannel laboratory
Subject: [BACKPORT R3.2] smb: client: harden channel selection on the 5.15 reconnect model

Backport the channel-eligibility intent of these upstream fixes:

  fc43a8ac396d302ced1e991e4913827cf72c8eb9
    cifs: cifs_pick_channel should try selecting active channels

  79280191c2fd7f24899bbd640003b5389d3c109c
    smb: client: fix cifs_pick_channel when channel needs reconnect

  663c28469d3274d6456f206a6671c91493d85ff1
    smb: client: fix cifs_pick_channel when channels are equally loaded

R3.1 already carries the rotated least-loaded selector derived from
ea90708d3cf3d0d92c02afe445ad463fb3c6bf10 and
66d590b828b1fd9fa337047ae58fe1c4c6f43609.

Backport note:
The CoreELEC vendor Linux 5.15 tree predates the later
ses->chans_need_reconnect bitmap and CIFS_CHAN_NEEDS_RECONNECT() helper.
It already tracks transport reconnect state per TCP_Server_Info through
server->tcpStatus. Use server->tcpStatus == CifsNeedReconnect as the 5.15
equivalent eligibility test for the current candidate (cur).

Keep the R3.1 start/cur rotation and least-loaded selection. Remove the
max_in_flight bookkeeping and equal-load fallback so a channel rejected by
the eligibility scan cannot be re-selected by the fallback. If no candidate
is eligible, index remains 0, preserving the upstream primary-channel
fallback behavior described by 663c28469.

No later reconnect-bitmap infrastructure or unrelated transport changes are
introduced by this backport.

--- a/fs/cifs/transport.c
+++ b/fs/cifs/transport.c
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 struct TCP_Server_Info *cifs_pick_channel(struct cifs_ses *ses)
 {
 	uint index = 0;
-	unsigned int min_in_flight = UINT_MAX, max_in_flight = 0;
+	unsigned int min_in_flight = UINT_MAX;
 	struct TCP_Server_Info *server = NULL;
 	int i, start, cur;
 
@@ -18,6 +18,9 @@
 				if (!server)
 					continue;
 
+				if (server->tcpStatus == CifsNeedReconnect)
+					continue;
+
 				/*
 				 * strictly speaking, we should pick up req_lock to read
 				 * server->in_flight. But it shouldn't matter much here if we
@@ -30,13 +33,7 @@
 					min_in_flight = server->in_flight;
 					index = cur;
 				}
-				if (server->in_flight > max_in_flight)
-					max_in_flight = server->in_flight;
 			}
-
-			/* if all channels are equally loaded, fall back to round-robin */
-			if (min_in_flight == max_in_flight)
-				index = (uint)start % ses->chan_count;
 		}
 		spin_unlock(&ses->chan_lock);
 		return ses->chans[index].server;
